        <section class="page-content">
            <h1>About Me</h1>

            <div class="bio-section">
                <h2>&#128100; Who I Am</h2>
                <p>Hi, I'm cerfly — a self-taught developer. No CS degree, no bootcamp; just curiosity, a Linux Mint machine, and the stubborn hunch that I can learn just about anything, one commit at a time.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="bio-section">
                <h2>&#128187; How I Learn</h2>
                <p>I learn by building. I picked vanilla HTML, CSS, and JavaScript because I wanted to understand the web from the ground up — no frameworks hiding the details. This site is my first real project. opencode — an AI assistant that doubles as a patient tutor and rubber duck in my terminal — writes the code; I decide what gets built, review what ships, and keep an eye on how it works. I won't pretend I read every line, but watching it code is honestly the part I enjoy most.</p>
                <p>My mantra is simple: build something, break something, fix it, then write down what I learned so I don't forget.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="bio-section">
                <h2>&#127793; Beyond Code</h2>
                <p>When the terminal closes, you'll find me exploring the outdoors, listening to music, or tinkering with something unrelated to computers. A curious mind doesn't clock out easily.</p>
            </div>
        </section>